<div class="template-columns"><article class="template-surface template-pad template-prose"><span class="template-kicker">The design principles</span><h2>Make the evidence easy to see.</h2><p>Birch’s interface separates sourced research, first-person experiences, and professional contributions. Those are different kinds of information, and readers should be able to tell them apart before relying on them.</p><div class="template-mini-grid"><a class="template-mini-card" href="/methodology"><BookOpen size={22} aria-hidden="true"/><h3>Research</h3><p>Original sources, scope, dates, and visible editorial status.</p></a><a class="template-mini-card" href="/design/commons-preview"><MessageSquare size={22} aria-hidden="true"/><h3>Experience</h3><p>A person’s account, with its context and clear limits.</p></a></div><h2 id="independence">Show who is speaking.</h2><p>Professional credentials, employment, company representation, and material interests need specific disclosures. Participation should not be confused with endorsement, and popularity should not be presented as evidence.</p><a class="template-context-link" href="/about">Read the current operator and ownership disclosure <ArrowUpRight size={15} aria-hidden="true"/></a><h2 id="corrections">Keep a path for corrections.</h2><p>The correction pattern starts with the exact statement, an explanation of the problem, and the supporting source. The eventual review should preserve history and make the outcome understandable.</p><a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/contribute?type=correction">Preview a correction draft</a><h2 id="boundaries">Be clear about limits.</h2><p>Source reading, editorial review, professional advice, and verification are separate steps. No interface label should promise one because another has happened.</p><p class="template-muted">This page is a layout specimen, not a replacement for Birch’s current policies or legal documents. The links below open those records.</p></article><aside class="template-context" aria-label="Standards navigation"><section><h2>About Birch</h2><a class="template-context-link" href="/about">About & operator disclosure <ArrowUpRight size={14} aria-hidden="true"/></a><a class="template-context-link" href="/methodology">Research methodology <ArrowUpRight size={14} aria-hidden="true"/></a><a class="template-context-link" href="/privacy">Privacy <ArrowUpRight size={14} aria-hidden="true"/></a><a class="template-context-link" href="/terms">Terms <ArrowUpRight size={14} aria-hidden="true"/></a></section><section><h2>On this page</h2><a class="template-context-link" href="#independence">Roles & relationships</a><a class="template-context-link" href="#corrections">Corrections</a><a class="template-context-link" href="#boundaries">Limits & policies</a></section><section><UserRound size={20} aria-hidden="true"/><h2>Bring useful expertise.</h2><p>Start with something you can explain, support, and put your name behind.</p><a class="template-context-link" href="/professionals">Professional contributions</a></section></aside></div>
